        "book_title": "2 Samuel",
        "book_short_title": "2 Sam.",
        "chapter_number": 14,
        "verse_number": 32,
        "verse_title": "2 Samuel 14:32",
        "verse_short_title": "2 Sam. 14:32",
        "scripture_text": "And Absalom answered Joab, Behold, I sent unto thee, saying, Come hither, that I may send thee to the king, to say, Wherefore am I come from Geshur? it had been good for me to have been there still: now therefore let me see the king's face; and if there be any iniquity in me, let him kill me."
