        "volume_title": "Old Testament",
        "book_title": "1 Kings",
        "book_short_title": "1 Kgs.",
        "chapter_number": 20,
        "verse_number": 32,
        "verse_title": "1 Kings 20:32",
        "verse_short_title": "1 Kgs. 20:32",
        "scripture_text": "So they girded sackcloth on their loins, and put ropes on their heads, and came to the king of Israel, and said, Thy servant Ben-hadad saith, I pray thee, let me live. And he said, Is he yet alive? he is my brother."
